  "notes": [
    "This chain runs GRANDPA: state_getStorage of Grandpa.CurrentSetId at B returns set 28, which this file records without a proof. Once a light client has imported B, these proofs check against the state root it stores for B.",
    "Revive.AccountInfoOf(0xa02ee16eb03d2cf1aef199f7658fb8c8e3188ffd) is a contract: trie id 0xbe307c2d11dbc9391cda93d17e9772542d1300c9af14e7431918fb49e2f47c3a, code hash 0xa72553f50cdf645fb343b2cf089e431a1b26fb07e80f4e2236d55bf9811c663f. Revive.CodeInfoOf of that hash says code_type Evm and code_len 899. eth_getCode returns EVM bytecode, which pallet-revive runs with REVM (899 B, starting 0x6080806040), and its keccak-256 is that code hash.",
    "state_getChildReadProof served 8 items: the 6 main-trie items that lead to the child root, exactly the items of childRoot.proof, and the 2 child-trie items in slot.proof.",
    "The EVM RPC's block 0x18aa3 is the Ethereum block the runtime built for B: its hash is Revive.BlockHash(B) and its parent hash Revive.BlockHash(B - 1), both proven at B. Its state root 0x56e81f171bcc55a6ff8345e692c0f86e5b48e01b996cadc001622fb5e363b421 is the empty-trie root, a placeholder, not B's.",
    "eth_getCode and eth_getStorageAt were asked at the EVM block's hash (EIP-1898). eth_getStorageAt returns the proven value byte for byte.",
    "slot.label is the text given with --label; this tool does not check it."
  ]
